.IX Title "Lucy::Index::PostingList 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Index::PostingList 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Index::PostingList \- Term\-Document pairings.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 9
\&    my $posting_list_reader 
\&        = $seg_reader\->obtain("Lucy::Index::PostingListReader");
\&    my $posting_list = $posting_list_reader\->posting_list( 
\&        field => \*(Aqcontent\*(Aq,
\&        term  => \*(Aqfoo\*(Aq,
\&    );
\&    while ( my $doc_id = $posting_list\->next ) {
\&        say "Matching doc id: $doc_id";
\&    }
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
PostingList is an iterator which supplies a list of document ids that match
a given term.
.PP
See IRTheory for definitions of “posting” and
“posting list”.
.SH "ABSTRACT METHODS"
.IX Header "ABSTRACT METHODS"
.SS get_doc_freq
.IX Subsection "get_doc_freq"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $posting_list\->get_doc_freq();
.Ve
.PP
Return the number of documents that the PostingList contains.  (This
number will include any documents which have been marked as deleted but
not yet purged.)
.SS seek
.IX Subsection "seek"
.Vb 2
\&    $posting_list\->seek($target);
\&    $posting_list\->seek();  # default: undef
.Ve
.PP
Prepare the PostingList object to iterate over matches for documents
that match \f(CW\*(C`target\*(C'\fR.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBtarget\fR \- The term to match.  If undef, the iterator will
be empty.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Index::PostingList isa Lucy::Search::Matcher isa Clownfish::Obj.
